ace from somewhere else in the  universe comes to the united states  if they came with nefarious goals it's  abundantly clear that at least at this  time  we would be able to do nothing to  prevent them from either killing all of  us or enslaving all of us or whatever so  for me  the national security analysis makes  more sense  if we're conceding that the most likely  explanation  is that this is either something from a  foreign power  in which case by the way if we really  don't understand what it is  then they are way further ahead than us  in many ways  and we should be extremely worried uh or  it's also possible that these  are unidentified or unknown to the  pilots and people that were interviewed  for the 60 minutes piece  but that it actually is classified at a  level above their  uh pay grade or level of access and the  people who know what these things are  did not participate uh because maybe 60  minutes doesn't even know who they are  so i i think my main point here is  for me the most serious approach to this  ufo uap  thing is first of all there is no  evidence that this is aliens from  somewhere other than earth there's just  no evidence of that and it's fascinating  to think of and i  understand the equations about the  probability of intelligent life other  than just  on earth earth and i recognize that if  we were ever to make that first contact  it would truly be an incredible thing  i'm not saying it's not possible i'm  just saying there's no evidence that  this is  that then it gets to the question of  assuming that it is indeed  man-made technology then  what is the source of it is it something  american that is so classified that even  the people interviewed don't know what  it is  uh or is it something foreign and then  you get the people who say well the  physics of it doesn't make sense  there were uh dissents in altitude  that would have killed any human body  that was in there  uh okay maybe there wasn't a human body  in there we also know  that the way a lot of these things are  filmed and perspective  and lenses can make something seem  different than what it might look like  to the naked eye  the where i come back to is  sort of an occam's razor type question  which is which of these explanations  require the fewest assumptions and the  ones that require the fewest assumptions  are  the visual perception that the pilots  claim is not entirely accurate that  would be a very straightforward way to  explain away a lot of this or  this is stuff that is known it's not  unidentified it was unidentified to the  pilots  and maybe to air traffic control but  it's  technology that higher up we are aware  of  or it was human-made technology from  some other place like the  from some other country the one that is  the furthest  and requires the most assumptions of  course would be the alien one which is  there is an alien species that is  advanced enough to travel  to earth from really far in the universe  because we've been observing the  universe that's more immediately around  us for a very long time  and to do it without any other signature  be it radio waves or whatever  else and right so the number of  assumptions start to go up  significantly so that's not where i am  on this now just one other thought on  this  one thing i read was the information  that was released  was fake information released by the us  government  to trick other countries what's the idea  here this is quite cynical  and if you go down this rabbit hole  the pilots interviewed on 60 minutes  could be in on it or not they might not  even be in on it the idea would be  let's make some video and have pilots  tell stories  or otherwise convince pilots of the  reality of this  so that 60 minutes we'll do a piece  we'll have some big reveal about these  uap ufos and  this will be seen by our adversaries and  it will completely misdirect them  so that they will start sinking r d  money into what they think they need to  do to develop  these things and it's just it's either  digital  it's not even real it's just been made  uh on a computer  um and it's a way to get adversaries to  spend money unfortunately  that's not totally implausible compared  to the alien theory uh  the the deliberate misdirection campaign  by  by the us government strikes me as more  plausible  send me your thoughts that's kind of  where my head is on this at this point  in time  most healthy granola bars have sort of a  bad reputation  because they're either dry or boring or  don't taste that good or  they don't satisfy your cravings but our  sponsor monk pack  is completely different because monk  pack  keto granola bars are sweet and  delicious  with a soft and chewy texture and yet  they have only 140 calories  one gram of sugar and only two to three  net carbs perfect  for the low sugar or keto diet they come  in  fantastic flavors like coconut cocoa  chip  blueberry almond vanilla and the new  flavor  peanut butter i've been a fan for a long  time i always have them in my pantry  it is a perfect snack and if you don't  love them as much as i do  you get all your money back they also  now have a subscription feature which i  love it'll save you 10 percent on every  order  and it ships automatically you'll get 20  off when you go to monkpack.com and use  the coupon code  pacman the link is right underneath this  video

